abyte-ci","id":17281578,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MjgxNTc4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17281578?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yugabyte-ci","html_url":"https://github.com/yugabyte-ci","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yugabyte-ci/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yugabyte-ci/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yugabyte-ci/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yugabyte-ci/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yugabyte-ci/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yugabyte-ci/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yugabyte-ci/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yugabyte-ci/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yugabyte-ci/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"event":"labeled","commit_id":null,"commit_url":null,"created_at":"2022-10-10T19:17:50Z","label":{"name":"priority/medium","color":"ffdc5e"},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/comments/1273721343","html_url":"https://github.com/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/14395#issuecomment-1273721343","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/14395","id":1273721343,"node_id":"IC_kwDOBlCVUc5L63H_","user":{"login":"deeps1991","id":21131754,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMTMxNzU0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21131754?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991","html_url":"https://github.com/deeps1991","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-10-10T19:22:52Z","updated_at":"2022-10-10T19:22:52Z","body":"Some additional notes from the code:\r\n\r\nIn `AbortTransaction` code, there is a call to `AtEOXact_Inval(false)` to invalidate caches. Here is the logic in performing cache invalidation:\r\n```\r\n/*                                                                              \r\n * AtEOXact_Inval                                                               \r\n *      Process queued-up invalidation messages at end of main transaction.     \r\n *                                                                              \r\n * If isCommit, we must send out the messages in our PriorCmdInvalidMsgs list   \r\n * to the shared invalidation message queue.  Note that these will be read      \r\n * not only by other backends, but also by our own backend at the next          \r\n * transaction start (via AcceptInvalidationMessages).  This means that         \r\n * we can skip immediate local processing of anything that's still in           \r\n * CurrentCmdInvalidMsgs, and just send that list out too.                      \r\n *                                                                              \r\n * If not isCommit, we are aborting, and must locally process the messages      \r\n * in PriorCmdInvalidMsgs.  No messages need be sent to other backends,         \r\n * since they'll not have seen our changed tuples anyway.  We can forget        \r\n * about CurrentCmdInvalidMsgs too, since those changes haven't touched         \r\n * the caches yet.                                                              \r\n *                                                                              \r\n * In any case, reset the various lists to empty.  We need not physically       \r\n * free memory here, since TopTransactionContext is about to be emptied         \r\n * anyway.                                                                      \r\n *                                                                              \r\n * Note:                                                                        \r\n *      This should be called as the last step in processing a transaction.     \r\n */                                                                             \r\nvoid                                                                            \r\nAtEOXact_Inval(bool isCommit)                                                   \r\n{                                                                               \r\n    ........\r\n    ........                                              \r\n    if (isCommit)                                                               \r\n    {                                                                           \r\n        .........                           \r\n                                                                         \r\n        AppendInvalidationMessages(&transInvalInfo->PriorCmdInvalidMsgs,        \r\n                                   &transInvalInfo->CurrentCmdInvalidMsgs);     \r\n                                                                                \r\n        ProcessInvalidationMessagesMulti(&transInvalInfo->PriorCmdInvalidMsgs,  \r\n                                         SendSharedInvalidMessages);            \r\n                                                                                \r\n        .........                              \r\n    }                                                                           \r\n    else                                                                        \r\n    {                                                                           \r\n        ProcessInvalidationMessages(&transInvalInfo->PriorCmdInvalidMsgs,       \r\n                                    LocalExecuteInvalidationMessage);                     \r\n    }                                                                           \r\n                                                                                \r\n    .....                                        \r\n}\r\n\r\n```\r\n\r\nNote that when a transaction is aborted, we only process cache invalidations issued up until the last call to `CommandCounterIncrement `(`PriorCmdInvalidMsgs`).\r\nThe comment above the function explicitly says that during abort we don't have to worry about what happened so far in the current command - but this doesn't seem to look right, from what I can see we do seem to be updating the caches.\r\n\r\nTo validate this theory, I tried calling `CommandCounterIncrement` right after `RenameRelationInternal`.\r\nConversely, I also tried removing the above `CommandCounterIncrement `and instead adding one more line to the above `AtEOXact_Inval `function to process invalidation messages for the current command as well.\r\n\r\nEither change fixes the issue.\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/comments/1273721343/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"deeps1991","id":21131754,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMTMxNzU0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21131754?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991","html_url":"https://github.com/deeps1991","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"id":7935900193,"node_id":"AE_lADOBlCVUc5TqVpKzwAAAAHZBDoh","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/events/7935900193","actor":{"login":"deeps1991","id":21131754,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMTMxNzU0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21131754?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991","html_url":"https://github.com/deeps1991","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"event":"assigned","commit_id":null,"commit_url":null,"created_at":"2022-12-01T21:53:51Z","assignee":{"login":"deeps1991","id":21131754,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMTMxNzU0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21131754?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991","html_url":"https://github.com/deeps1991","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/comments/1334497693","html_url":"https://github.com/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/14395#issuecomment-1334497693","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/14395","id":1334497693,"node_id":"IC_kwDOBlCVUc5PitGd","user":{"login":"deeps1991","id":21131754,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMTMxNzU0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21131754?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991","html_url":"https://github.com/deeps1991","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-12-01T21:57:49Z","updated_at":"2022-12-01T21:58:41Z","body":"Update: Tested the same erroneous case on upstream postgres, and this error did not occur there. This is because only YB performs aggressive caching, i.e. we update the cache as soon as we try to update/insert tuples into the PG catalog.\r\nTherefore this comment in PG code:\r\n```\r\n * If not isCommit, we are aborting, and must locally process the messages      \r\n * in PriorCmdInvalidMsgs.  No messages need be sent to other backends,         \r\n * since they'll not have seen our changed tuples anyway.  We can forget        \r\n * about CurrentCmdInvalidMsgs too, since those changes haven't touched         \r\n * the caches yet. \r\n ```\r\nis true for upstream PG but not for YB. We should process invalidation messages for both prior and current commands.\r\ncc @m-iancu ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/comments/1334497693/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"deeps1991","id":21131754,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMTMxNzU0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21131754?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991","html_url":"https://github.com/deeps1991","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps1991/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deeps